==Icelandic==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|svá|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|swe|lang=is}} and {{proto|Indo-European|se|lang=is}}. Cognate with Old English {{term|swa|swā|lang=ang}} (English {{term|so|lang=en}}), Old Frisian {{term|sa}}, Old Saxon {{term|so|sō}} (Dutch {{term|zo}}), Old High German {{term|so|sō|lang=goh}} (German {{term|so|lang=de}}), Swedish {{term|så|lang=sv}}), Danish {{term|så|lang=da}}, Gothic {{term|𐍃𐍅𐌰}}, Latin {{term|si|lang=la}} (from an earlier form {{term|suad|lang=la}}), Oscan {{term|svai|svaí}}, Umbrian {{term|sve}}, Greek {{term|ὡς}} (earlier '''*ϝος''').

